  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​808 — October 27, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192048/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0 12px;\"><p>JavaScript Weekly</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191993/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/d78ifnbyoegacu1b82sf.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191993/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"tanstack.com\">TanStack AI 1.0: The Vendor-Neutral AI Toolkit Goes Stable</a></span> — TanStack's framework-agnostic AI toolkit reaches 1.0, with stable APIs for chat, tools and media, plus 23 provider adapters. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191994/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">A new agent harness</a> supports long-running sessions, but its APIs remain experimental.</p>\n<p>Tuzlak, Herrington, et al. (TanStack) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191992/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"110\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/03592c49.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"110\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191992/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.meticulous.ai\">Would You Let Your AI Agent Grade Its Own Homework?</a></span> — Agents write code faster than ever. They even review their own work. But who’s reviewing them? Dropbox, Notion &amp; ElevenLabs don’t take the risk. With Meticulous, every change is exhaustively verified, with zero developer effort.</p>\n<p>Meticulous <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191995/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"devblogs.microsoft.com\">Announcing TypeScript 7.1 Beta</a></span> — TypeScript 7 gets <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192049/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">a programmatic API</a>, plus 'content mappers', a plugin point for checking code embedded in files such as Vue, Svelte, and Astro components. Also new are <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192050/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">source phase imports</a> and <code>--target es2026</code>.</p>\n<p>Daniel Rosenwasser (Microsoft) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191996/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.bram.us\">GTA.js: 1997's <em>Grand Theft Auto</em>, But in JavaScript</a></span> — Bramus has been reimplementing the original top-down GTA's engine in JavaScript and WebGL, loading Liberty City from the game's original demo files. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191997/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Play it here</a>.</p>\n<p>Bramus Van Damme </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 Fittingly, Pat Kerr, whose 1996 Atari ST prototype formed the basis of the original game's vehicle physics, recently <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191998/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">rebuilt it in JavaScript</a>.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Deno's Bartek Iwańczuk says the team is <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191999/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">working on getting Deno into a foundation</a>. Meanwhile, a new fork, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192000/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Ende</a>, plans to drop Node compatibility and refocus on sandboxing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192001/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Safari 27.1 previews the Device Posture and Viewport Segments APIs</a> behind feature flags on the iPhone Duo, letting JavaScript detect folds and inspect screen segments.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192002/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Chrome 156 has reached stable</a> and no longer caches module fetch failures, so a dynamic <code>import()</code> that fails due to a network or HTTP error can be retried.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>RELEASES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192003/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Node.js v26.12.1 (Current)</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192004/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">v24.22.1 (LTS)</a> and <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192005/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">v22.23.4</a> – Security releases fixing ten CVEs, including the <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192006/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">'Node2Shell' Brotli decoder flaw</a>, which can lead to remote code execution when an app decompresses malicious data. <em>(Also, Node 26 is due to become LTS tomorrow.)</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192007/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Bun 1.4.4</a> – Adds <code>bun fmt</code>, a Prettier-compatible formatter that uses your existing Prettier or oxfmt config. It's <em>very</em> fast.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192008/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Electron 45</a> – Upgrades to Chromium 156, Node 24.22 and V8 15.6, and adds hooks for the <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192009/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Prompt API</a> so apps can plug in a local model.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192010/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">pnpm 12.16</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192011/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Remix 3.1</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192012/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">axios 1.21</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192013/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Deno 2.9.8</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📖  Articles and Videos</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192014/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"t3.at\">Parser Combinators in TypeScript, Built From Scratch</a></span> — Parser combinators sit between regexes and heavyweight tools like tree-sitter. This animated, step-by-step walkthrough shows the basic elements of building them, concluding in an example turning <code>ping</code> output into typed objects.</p>\n<p>Florian Schindler </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192015/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"tkdodo.eu\">Dead Code Shouldn't Exist: How Sentry Cut 28,000 Lines</a></span> — A talk Dominik has given at six conferences this year, now as swipeable slides with a full transcript. He covers how unused code can cost more than you might think, and how Sentry used <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192016/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Knip</a> to remove 28,000 lines.</p>\n<p>Dominik Dorfmeister (Sentry) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192025/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"lp.jetbrains.com\">AI.js Day 2026: Frontend's Scariest AI Questions, Live on Channel 13, Nov 13</a></span> — No hype, just the AI questions frontend devs are afraid to ask. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192025/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Save your spot</a>.</p>\n<p>JetBrains <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192018/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.master.dev\">Building an Isolated Preview for AI-Generated HTML</a></span> — Rendering model-written HTML in a <code>srcdoc</code> iframe runs it on your own origin. A security engineer breaks the naive approach, then rebuilds it using <code>sandbox</code> and a strict CSP, with demos showing what each one blocks.</p>\n<p>Keshav Malik </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192019/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"jovidecroock.com\">A First Look at TypeScript 7.1's Content Mappers</a></span> — TypeScript 7 ignores tsserver plugins, but 7.1's content mappers can turn non-TS files into TypeScript. Here's how they work, applied to CSS modules and <code>.graphql</code> files.</p>\n<p>Jovi De Croock </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192020/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">How Engines Turn Dynamic Objects Into Fast Field Access</a> – Shapes and inline caches, explained with runnable sketches. <cite>Max Bernstein</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192021/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Software is Slow Because of Bad Design, Not Slow Languages</a> <cite>Sean Goedecke (GitHub)</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠 Code &amp; Tools</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192022/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/lvhon6ibgjv0prddvf5z.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192022/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"structs.arv.tools\">Structs: TC39's Shared Structs Proposal, But Usable Today</a></span> — A former TC39 delegate's implementation of the Stage 2 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192023/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">structs proposal</a>. The idea is you get shared memory between workers, so threads can work on the same objects instead of serializing copies back and forth. There's a <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192024/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">playground</a> too.</p>\n<p>Erik Arvidsson </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192026/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"tanstack.com\">Introducing TanStack Redact: A Slimmer React Runtime</a></span> — A build plugin swaps React and React DOM for a smaller reimplementation in the browser with no code changes. It works with Vite, Start, Vinext and Next.js, and while TanStack reports 20-70% smaller client builds, rendering is <em>synchronous only</em>.</p>\n<p>Tanner Linsley (TanStack) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192017/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"wallabyjs.com\">AI Tests That Catch Real Bugs</a></span> — AI can write low-value tests that pass without checking much. Wallaby helps your agent refine assertions and catch bugs.</p>\n<p>Wallaby Team <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192027/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">Verdaccio 7.0: The Self-Hosted npm Registry Adds Staged Publishing and 2FA</a></span> — A mature, lightweight way to self-host your own npm registry and proxy. v7 adds experimental staged publishing (where new versions need approval before going live) and 2FA, plus stricter ownership checks.</p>\n<p>Verdaccio Team </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192028/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"biomejs.dev\">Biome 2.6 Adds Markdown, YAML and SCSS Support</a></span> — The Rust-powered alternative to Prettier and ESLint adds formatting support for Markdown, YAML and SCSS, along with initial linting support. JavaScript plugins for custom lint rules are available as a developer preview.</p>\n<p>Biome Core Team </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>☕ <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192029/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">CoffeeScript 2.7.1</a> – The first release in four and a half years brings Node 22+ fixes and <code>with { type: 'json' }</code> import attributes.</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 If you never used <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192030/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">CoffeeScript</a>, it is/was a Ruby- and Python-flavored language that compiled to JavaScript. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192031/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Brendan Eich held up its arrow functions and lightweight classes</a> as models for what went into ES6 (ES2015).</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192032/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">oxlint 1.89</a> – The Rust-based linter now counts the upstream recommended rules of its React, Vue, Next.js, Jest/Vitest, and other plugins as 'recommended' so expect more reports if you upgrade.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192037/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Mutative 2.0</a> – Immer-style efficient immutable updates library. The author reports a 3.6x speedup over Immer across a benchmark suite.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192035/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">SonicJS 3.0</a> – Headless CMS for Cloudflare Workers, built on Hono. v3 rebuilds the data layer, auth and plugin system. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192036/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Homepage</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192033/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">query-string 10.0</a> – Parse and stringify URL query strings. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192034/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Now throws for values it can't represent</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192038/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">ShareDB 7.0</a> – Realtime database backend based on operational transformation.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📱 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192039/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Expo is mobile AI infrastructure</a>. Your agent writes the code, and Expo gets your iOS and Android app built and into the stores. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192039/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Try it</a>.</p>\n<p>🧩 CAPTCHAs can frustrate real users and cost you conversions. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192040/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Try Fingerprint’s bot detection for free</a> and stop abuse without the friction.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>🔒 <strong>Node2Shell:</strong> <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192006/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">ELLIO now reports exploit traffic in the wild</a> for the Brotli RCE fixed in the Node releases (as mentioned earlier). The flaw is in Google's Brotli library, so <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192041/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">bundled copies elsewhere need patching too</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Sentry has <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192042/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">given $1m to open source maintainers this year</a>. JavaScript recipients include pnpm, TanStack, MSW, Knip and three Three.js maintainers, plus the OpenJS Foundation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🎉 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192043/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">CSS-Tricks, the popular web dev resource, is independent again</a>, now owned by longtime editor Geoff Graham.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Arc, the design-led Chromium browser popular with developers, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192044/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">is being sunset</a> with The Browser Company steering everyone to <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192045/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Dia</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📄 Google Docs <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192046/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">can now open, edit and collaborate on Markdown files natively</a> and Drive renders previews of them too.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
